Jonas and I walk through the office.
He shows me my desk.
"This is your space, Maya," Jonas says.
I put my backpack on the floor.
A chair is already there.
I take my laptop out of the backpack.
"You have a laptop and a chair," Jonas says.
"Yes, I have that," I answer.
Jonas looks at the desk.
"We still need things for you," he says.
"You have no monitor and no keyboard."
I nod.
"I need a monitor," I say.
"And maybe a mouse?" Jonas asks.
"Yes, I need a mouse too," I answer.
Jonas counts on his fingers.
"One, two, three," he says.
"One monitor, one keyboard, and one mouse."
He notes the three things.
"I am ordering that for you now," Jonas says.
